### 1. Check Voting Eligibility Q1
Given a person's age as an integer, evaluate whether they meet the legal qualification threshold to vote. A citizen is
eligible to vote if their age is 18 years or older.
Input: A single integer representing age. | Output: Print Eligible if age ≥ 18, else print Not Eligible.
TEST CASE 1
Input: 20 Output: Eligible
TEST CASE 2
Input: 15 Output: Not Eligible
